content.text:
Now fix the intro crash. In game.loop intro block:
```
if (this.mode === 'intro' && this.intro) {
  this.intro.update(raw);
  this.introTime += raw;
  if (this.input.skip && this.introTime > 1.2) this.intro.finish();
  this.ui.update(raw);
  this.renderer.render(this.intro.scene, this.intro.camera);
  this.input.endFrame();
  return;
}
```
After finish, this.intro null. Fix:
```
const intro = this.intro;
if (this.mode === 'intro' && intro) {
  intro.update(raw);
  ...
  if (...) intro.finish();
  this.ui.update(raw);
  if (this.intro && this.mode === 'intro') this.renderer.render(intro.scene,intro.camera);
  this.input.endFrame();
  return;
}
```
If endIntro runs inside intro.update, this.intro null and mode play; but we should still not render intro. Then return next frame. Also `this.intro.update(raw)` may call finish at end and then `this.introTime += raw` fine. Use local. Patch.

Also in `endIntro`, `this.intro?.dispose(); this.intro = null;` fine. Add `this.input.endFrame()`? Already after loop. But if `endIntro` called outside loop (maybe), key press remains. Not needed. But in loop we need endFrame after finish; yes.

Let's patch.

